@@Zortex in five minutes
@@Talk
@Talks

Plain-text notes, projects and a calendar, in Neovim and on the web.
This note is also a slide deck: open it on the web and click **slides**.

# Why
## Notes are structure
Every heading, bold heading and label is a section, so a link can point
anywhere: [Projects/#2 Learning] or [Sourdough/#Method/:Bake].

- One format for notes, tasks and the calendar
- Readable without any tool
- Links by name, not by path

Notes:
- The web app and Neovim share one parser, tested against the same fixtures
- Ask who already keeps notes in plain text

## The loop @steps
- Objectives say what matters this quarter
- Projects say what to do about it
  - their tasks carry `@size`, so progress and XP follow
- The calendar says when

# How
## The plan, drawn
![./images/loop.svg]

## Math
Time on a task in hours is $t = \frac{\text{XP}}{10}$, and over a season

$$
\text{progress} = \sum_{o} w_o \cdot \frac{\text{done}_o}{\text{total}_o}
$$

## Try it
```sh
zortex serve -dir doc/example
```
Then open this note and press `s` on the slides for the presenter window.
